WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
We categorize choking into two levels

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.060
based on how much air is getting through.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.140
In a mild choking situation,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.300
the person is still able to move some air

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.060
in and out of their lungs.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.780
You will usually see them coughing forcefully,

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.840
and they might even be able to speak or cry briefly.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.260
The best thing you can do here is stay calm

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.059
and encourage them to keep coughing

00:00:22.059 --> 00:00:24.900
as hard as they can to expel the item.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.139
You wanna let their body do the work.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.820
However, stay close and watch them carefully

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.419
because if that forceful coughing fails

00:00:33.419 --> 00:00:35.500
and the blockage stays put,

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.040
it can quickly turn into severe choking.

